 - [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission's base revision matches the visit's latest revision, the system SHALL accept the submission and create a new revision with revision number base + 1.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission's base revision does not match the visit's latest revision, the system SHALL reject the submission and return the current latest revision and its payload.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When two or more accepted submissions share the same base revision, the system SHALL mark the visit as having unresolved review work and return all competing revisions in the retrieval response.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a visit has unresolved review work, the system SHALL return null for the resolved payload in the retrieval response.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a coordinator submits a resolution with base revision equal to the latest revision and a resolvedFrom list, the system SHALL accept it as a new revision, mark the listed revisions as superseded, and clear the competing revisions set.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a visit has no competing revisions, the system SHALL return the latest revision's payload as the resolved payload in the retrieval response.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: The system SHALL validate that a submission's plot reference exists in the site catalog before accepting it.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: The system SHALL validate that a submission's observation date, observer list, species cover estimates, and notes conform to their declared types before accepting it.
